\f1\fs26 Sarah spent the rest of the morning gathering everything known about Anthony Hardy. 
\f2\i Everything
\f1\i0 , however, amounted to very little. The spaces where data had once been were as obvious as toothache to her. Much was recently deleted, as recent as this morning. No matter how deep she dug, all she uncovered regarding Anthony (Tony, Cracker) Hardy was: a birth certificate (
\f2\i father unknown
\f1\i0 ), patchy school records (noting his obstreperousness in the face of poor grades), a listing for Cracker Jack Cleaning (no business address), and some fines for drunk and disorderly. There were no consumer records. There was no evidence of any marketing advertising algorithms apprising him worthy of spamming. Sarah raised her eyebrow when she searched for malware attacks against him and found none.\
Was Mr Fairy Boxers too dull to surveil? \
Sarah stared out the window with a blank thousand-metre stare. On another day, she might have shrugged off a visit from a creepy agent. She could handle those, but the cleaner couldn\'92t mend his own overalls. He\'92d be no match for Agent Jones. Sarah would have to warn him.\
When 1:30pm approached, she took a hover-copt to the clinic where she gave samples, underwent embarrassing and probing examinations. A colony of scanners bombarded her with a broad spectrum of radiation. As expected, she was in perfect health, and therefore approved for promotion.\
One result gave her cause for reflection.\
\
PREGNANCY: negative\
\
It was more than a decade since she resolved she would never\'97could never\'97fall pregnant.\
\
Sarah went home and resumed searching for Mr Fairy Boxers\'97a home address, or even a regular watering hole. On an impulse borne of desperation, she gathered a cloak, tied her hair back, and called a hover-copt for The Ghetto, where she did the rounds of bars where vanilla Cloudborne mixed with the Elvi. A nagging hunch\'97or perhaps the only drive she could raise enthusiasm for\'97suggested Mr Fairy Boxers might enjoy karaoke.\
Her dim hunch ignited into a solid lead at the 
\f2\i Viva Vegas Club
\f1\i0  where a waiter named Elvine knew the names \'91Cracker Jack Cleaning\'92 and \'91Cracker Hardy\'92, and was familiar with the tear in his overalls.\
\'93Go check out the 
\f2\i Stick it Inn
\f1\i0 , sugar,\'94 Elvine told Sarah. \'93That\'92s where his bodyguards usually hole him up.\'94\
\
Sarah found Cracker at the 
\f2\i Stick it Inn
\f1\i0 , flanked by three scruffs who looked like a pirate, a fence and a contract killer. Bodyguards indeed. Not long after, the bomb exploded.\

